# MAKE LINEAGE ACTUALLY WORK END-TO-END IN PRODUCTION ON FIREBASE.

The final production URL remains:

```text
https://family-tree-a4c4f.web.app/
```

## Production Firebase Web App

First check whether a Firebase Web App now exists in project:

```text
family-tree-a4c4f
```

Do not create a duplicate.

If an app exists, retrieve its official Firebase Web configuration.

If none exists and Firebase Management API quota now permits registration, register exactly one Web App named:

```text
Lineage
```

If HTTP 429 still prevents registration, do not hammer the API. Record the blocker and continue everything that can still be completed locally.

When Web configuration becomes available, wire the exact official config into the existing modular Firebase browser bridge.

Do not invent or manually guess:

```text
apiKey
appId
messagingSenderId
storageBucket
```

Do not commit any Admin SDK private credentials.

Firebase Web configuration is client initialization configuration; Firebase Admin/service-account credentials remain strictly server-side.

## Firebase Authentication

Complete the actual browser integration.

The production frontend must use Firebase Authentication for:

```text
registration
login
logout
authentication persistence
password reset
email verification where required
```

Use the already-created modular Firebase client bridge.

Make Firebase Auth the authoritative identity system.

The application must no longer rely on PostgreSQL sessions or Express sessions.

Application startup must become:

```text
page load
→ Firebase initialize
→ Firebase Auth resolve
→ authenticated user → application
→ no user → login/register
→ failure → recovery UI
```

An authentication failure must never produce a blank page.

Complete real frontend ID-token propagation to Firebase Functions.

Protected API requests must obtain:

```javascript
await user.getIdToken()
```

and send:

```text
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

Functions must continue deriving identity from verified Firebase tokens, never from browser-supplied `userId` values.

## Cloud Storage

Check whether the production default Firebase Storage bucket now exists.

If it exists, retrieve the real bucket identifier and configure the client.

Do not invent the bucket URL.

Complete the production photo flow:

```text
select image
→ validate image
→ Firebase Storage
→ Firestore photo metadata/path
→ display image
```

Support:

```text
upload
display
replace
delete
cleanup after person deletion
```

Do not use:

```text
public/uploads
Render filesystem
Cloud Run filesystem
Firestore binary blobs
```

Keep the already-tested Storage security model.

## Tree Frontend

Functions implementation alone is no longer enough.

Connect the real frontend UI to the Firebase backend.

Verify through the actual browser interface:

```text
tree load
tree rename
person create
person edit
person delete
relationship create
relationship delete
page refresh
```

Every successful write must persist after reload.

## Feature Parity

Open:

```text
docs/FIREBASE_FEATURE_PARITY_MATRIX.md
```

Every remaining feature currently marked FAIL, PARTIAL, PENDING, or NOT COMPLETE must now be resolved into exactly one of:

```text
PASS
FAIL
NOT APPLICABLE
BLOCKED BY EXTERNAL/HUMAN ACTION
```

Do not leave vague intermediate states.

For each feature, inspect the latest intended pre-Firebase application before deciding whether it is actually required.

Specifically resolve:

```text
sharing
approval
payments
memories
evidence
import
export
```

If a feature belongs to the intended current Lineage product, migrate it.

If it is old/abandoned functionality, mark it NOT APPLICABLE and document the repository evidence.

Do not build unused legacy features merely because old code exists.

Do not silently drop a current feature.

## Sharing

If current, implement secure tree membership.

Authorization must work at both:

```text
Firebase Functions
Firestore Rules
```

Test at least:

```text
owner
authorized member
unauthorized user
```

Add editor/viewer roles only if the actual product requires them.

## Approval

If account approval is current, preserve it.

Firebase Authentication means:

```text
identity verified
```

It does not necessarily mean:

```text
Lineage account approved
```

If approval is required, enforce it server-side.

## Payments

If M-Pesa/payment functionality is still part of Lineage, move all trusted processing into Firebase Functions.

Never expose payment credentials in frontend JavaScript.

Secrets must remain server-side.

If payment functionality is no longer part of the intended current product, explicitly mark it NOT APPLICABLE.

## Memories and Evidence

If these are current Lineage features, complete their Firestore/Storage model, Functions authorization, frontend CRUD, and security tests.

If not current, mark them NOT APPLICABLE with evidence.

## Import and Export

If current, finish both.

Import must never trust an owner UID contained inside an uploaded file.

Authenticated ownership must be assigned server-side.

Validate:

```text
people
relationships
references
duplicates
format
authorization
```

Export must expose only trees the authenticated user is authorized to access.

Where practical test:

```text
export tree
→ import into clean emulator state
→ compare persons and relationships
```

## Emulator Final Gate

Before production deployment, run the complete Firebase suite again.

Required:

```text
Auth Emulator
Firestore Emulator
Functions Emulator
Storage Emulator
Hosting Emulator
```

Run:

```text
npm run test:firebase
npm run test:firebase:rules
```

plus all other applicable Firebase tests.

Create two emulator accounts and prove again that User A cannot access User B's:

```text
tree
persons
relationships
photos
private feature data
```

Cross-user isolation failure blocks deployment.

## End-to-End Emulator Test

Perform a realistic browser flow.

Create User A.

Register/login.

Create a tree.

Create multiple family members across at least three generations.

Create parent-child and spouse relationships.

Upload a photo.

Reload the browser.

Confirm persistence.

Edit a person.

Delete a relationship.

Logout.

Login again.

Confirm data remains.

Then create User B and verify User B cannot access User A's data.

